            {
              "text": "When handling probate and deceased estate administration in Brisbane East and the Bayside (specifically around Wynnum and Carindale), there are several well-regarded local and specialist law firms that can assist you:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Carindale & Adjacent Suburbs (Carina / Morningside)**\n\n* **Willwise (Carindale)**  \n  * **Focus:** Specialised succession and estate law boutique.  \n  * **Highlights:** Led by Judy Hayward, a **Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialist in Succession Law**. They specifically handle Applications for Grants of Probate, Letters of Administration, calling in assets, and full deceased estate administration. They also offer home visits across Brisbane East and Redlands.\n* **Grasic Lawyers (Carina – Old Cleveland Road)**  \n  * **Focus:** General and estate practice located right next to Carindale.  \n  * **Highlights:** Regularly guides executors through Queensland Supreme Court probate applications, transmissions of real property, and final distributions to beneficiaries.\n* **Fulljames Law (Morningside / Brisbane East)**  \n  * **Focus:** Deceased estates, probate, and estate administration.  \n  * **Highlights:** Transparent pricing with structured fixed-fee probate packages and support tailored to executors who want full-service administration or just help with obtaining the grant.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Wynnum & Bayside**\n\n* **Connor Hunter Lawyers (Wynnum & Cleveland)**  \n  * **Focus:** Full-service local law firm with a dedicated Wills & Estates team.  \n  * **Highlights:** Established in 1971 with deep roots in Wynnum. Highly experienced in Queensland probate, managing deceased estates, calling in bank accounts/shares, and dealing with real estate transfers in the Bayside area.\n* **Queensland Legal Practice (Wynnum – Bay Terrace)**  \n  * **Focus:** Local practice offering wills, probate, and estate administration.  \n  * **Highlights:** Conveniently located in central Wynnum; regularly assists local executors with court filings, advertising requirements, and estate settlements.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Nearby Bayside Hubs (Capalaba & Cleveland)**\n*(Useful if the deceased held property across the Redlands/Bayside corridor)*\n\n* **McCarthy Durie Lawyers (MDL) (Capalaba & Cleveland)**  \n  * **Focus:** One of the largest and most established practices in the Brisbane Bayside area.  \n  * **Highlights:** Comprehensive estate administration team capable of handling simple probate applications as well as complex multi-property estates or business distributions.\n* **Macfie Curlewis Spiro (Capalaba)**  \n  * **Focus:** Longstanding local firm with a strong wills, probate, and estate administration practice.  \n  * **Highlights:** Well-versed in assisting executors with both small estates and contested/complex distributions.\n\n---\n\n### **Questions to Ask When Choosing a Firm as an Executor:**\n1. **Fee Structure:** Do they offer a **fixed fee** for obtaining the Grant of Probate, and what is their billing structure for the ongoing estate administration (hourly vs. capped)?\n2. **Scope of Representation:** Can you engage them simply to obtain the Grant of Probate (leaving you to distribute the funds), or can they take over the entire process (closing accounts, handling tax returns, and distributing assets)?\n3. **Property Transfers:** If the deceased owned real estate in Queensland, ask if the firm can handle the **Transmission Application** through Titles Queensland alongside the probate process.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
